-- allium: 3
-- 17-bond-pricing.allium

-- Scope: Valuation of fixed-coupon bonds with bullet redemption, and of the
--   same bonds with an issuer call (callable bonds) (D-022, D-046).
-- Includes: what a valuation needs, what it must return (including the
--   quoting measures and the default-risk inputs of spec 11), how the issuer
--   credit curve and the rate model are used, how life-cycle events are
--   handled, how the planner expands a bond request.
-- Excludes:
--   - The trade and security payload fields: generated from the Julia types
--     (D-018); static data enters through spec 16.
--   - Curves, the issuer credit curve, the swaption cube and the Hull-White
--     calibration themselves (08).
--   - Sensitivities and FRTB aggregation (11): bumped graph nodes (D-032).
--   - Floating-rate, amortising, inflation-linked, convertible and putable
--     bonds; make-whole calls (see PlainVanillaOnly).
-- Dependencies: 01, 02, 03, 08.
--
-- Planning (D-020), one pass, for one bond position version:
--   calendars named by the security (03) -> discount curve of the bond's
--   currency (08) -> issuer credit curve for issuer and seniority (08,
--   prerequisite: discount curve) -> for a callable bond also the swaption
--   cube and the Hull-White calibration in the bond's currency (08,
--   prerequisite: discount curve) -> valuation node (this spec). The market
--   price series of the security, when one exists, is an input of the
--   valuation node.

use "./01-bitemporal-data.allium" as data
use "./02-calculation-graph.allium" as graph

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

contract BondValuation {
    value: (position: data/InputVersion, security: data/InputVersion, as_of: Timestamp, discount_curve: String, credit_curve: String, rate_model: String?, market_price: data/InputVersion?, calendars: Set<data/InputVersion>, reporting_currencies: Set<String>, fx: Set<String>) -> String

    @invariant ScheduleFromTerms
        -- The coupon schedule comes from the security's terms via the
        -- calendar contract (03): coupon dates, frequency, day count,
        -- business day adjustment, first and last stubs, payment lags.

    @invariant RiskyDiscounting
        -- Each cashflow is discounted on the risk-free curve of the bond's
        -- currency and weighted by the survival probability from the credit
        -- curve of its issuer and seniority; the recovery on default is part
        -- of that credit curve object (08), so the valuation and the default
        -- risk charge (11) read one credit view (D-046). An issuer with no credit
        -- curve is a deterministic rejection naming the issuer, never a
        -- silent default of the spread (proxy rule: open question in 08).

    @invariant BulletRedemption
        -- Redemption is the whole notional at maturity at par, together with
        -- the last coupon. Cashflows paying on as_of are included ("for
        -- value", D-033).

    @invariant CallableByHullWhite
        -- A callable bond is the straight bond less the issuer's call option.
        -- The call option is valued on a one-factor Hull-White lattice whose
        -- volatility is calibrated to the swaption cube (08) at each run and
        -- whose mean reversion is fixed by the model recipe, a configuration
        -- artefact reviewed with the model (D-054); the call schedule (European
        -- or Bermudan), the notice periods and the call prices come from the
        -- terms. The straight bond inside the same lattice must reproduce the
        -- straight-bond PV within the recipe's tolerance, or the valuation is
        -- rejected (consistency of the lattice with the curve).

    @invariant DeterministicLattice
        -- The lattice has a number of steps fixed by the recipe, never chosen
        -- adaptively; evaluation is single-threaded and reproducible (02,
        -- DeterministicComputation). Rounding follows the canonical rounding
        -- (D-015); prescribed formulas follow their source exactly and cite
        -- it (F-3).

    @invariant SeasonedBondsAreOpenOnly
        -- Cashflows paid before as_of play no part. A bond past its final
        -- payment at as_of is a deterministic rejection saying it matured
        -- (the position should have been closed by a succession, D-023). In
        -- a batch run the matured position is excluded and listed as an
        -- explicit exclusion naming the position (16, ExplicitExclusions), so
        -- that someone closes it and the run is not stopped (D-054).

    @invariant LifeCycleThroughSuccession
        -- Partial redemption (notional reduction), exercise of a call,
        -- redemption at maturity, issuer change and amendment arrive as
        -- successions of the position (D-023); the valuation always uses the
        -- position version effective at as_of. An issuer default arrives as
        -- a succession into a defaulted position, valued at a recovery price
        -- (an input) plus the accrued claim, and leaves the credit-curve
        -- valuation; a called bond that is not yet redeemed remains a bond,
        -- valued to its call date at the call price, until a succession
        -- records the redemption (D-054).

    @invariant ResultShape
        -- The valuation result contains (D-046): PV in local currency (the
        -- position currency) and in each requested reporting currency with the
        -- FX object used (D-033); clean and dirty price per 100 of nominal and
        -- as amounts; accrued interest; the cashflow table (accrual start and
        -- end, payment date, notional, year fraction as exact rational,
        -- coupon, discount factor, survival probability, PV in local
        -- currency); yield to maturity under the convention named in the
        -- terms; for callable bonds also the straight-bond PV, the option
        -- value, the option-adjusted spread and the lattice recipe hash;
        -- and the basis of the credit curve used (quoted CDS, bond-implied
        -- or proxy, with the proxy key when it is a proxy, 08).
        -- When a market price exists: the z-spread (straight bond) and the
        -- option-adjusted spread (callable) that reproduce that price on the
        -- risk-free curve. Without a market price these are reported as absent
        -- with the reason, never as zero and never as a rejection.

    @invariant DefaultRiskInputs
        -- The result carries the inputs spec 11 needs for the default risk
        -- charge, so no second valuation is made: issuer, seniority, the
        -- recovery rate used, notional, and the fair value (dirty PV in local
        -- currency) as the basis for the jump-to-default amount.

    @invariant InformationalRiskMeasures
        -- Effective duration, convexity and PV01 are reported for desks. They
        -- are informational: regulatory sensitivities always come from the
        -- prescribed shocked graph nodes (D-032) and never from these figures.

    @invariant YieldConventionNamed
        -- The yield to maturity is computed under the convention named in
        -- the terms (its edition included); the formula follows its source
        -- document exactly (F-3). The default convention is yield compounded
        -- at the coupon frequency on the bond's day count, from the clean
        -- price (D-054); the terms of a bond may name another.

    @invariant PlainVanillaOnly
        -- v1 (D-046): fixed coupon, constant notional until a succession,
        -- single currency, bullet redemption at par, no ex-coupon period,
        -- call prices stated in the terms (no make-whole). Other terms are a
        -- deterministic rejection naming the feature.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

actor PricingWorker {
    identified_by: data/User
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

surface BondValuationComputation {
    facing worker: PricingWorker

    contracts:
        demands BondValuation
        demands graph/DeterministicComputation

    @guarantee GoldenCrossCheck
        -- Golden bullet and callable bond valuations are reproduced
        -- independently (QuantLib, D-010) within a stated tolerance before a
        -- model version can enter a production release. Property checks that
        -- hold without a reference: a callable bond is never worth more than
        -- the same straight bond; a call price far above the straight value
        -- makes the option worthless; shifting the credit curve to zero
        -- spread gives the risk-free PV.

    @guarantee UpstreamContribution
        -- The lattice engine, the callable bond and the yield conventions are
        -- generic and live in a separate package free of Veridian
        -- dependencies, offered to JuliaActuary first (D-031).
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Resolved (D-046): risky discounting with the issuer credit curve; Hull-White
-- one-factor lattice for calls; result shape as above, including default-risk
-- inputs and informational risk measures.
-- Resolved (D-054): default yield convention is compounded at coupon
-- frequency on the bond day count from the clean price; an issuer default is
-- a succession and a called bond stays a bond until redeemed; a matured bond
-- is excluded and listed; Hull-White volatility is calibrated and mean
-- reversion fixed by recipe.
open question "Which edition of the yield convention does the bank quote by in each market, and which markets need a convention other than the default?"
open question "Hull-White mean reversion value and the number of lattice steps and tolerance per currency: the recipe's values, to be set when the model is validated (21)."
